1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,790
Welcome to Webb Cubing Club.

2
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:05,390
Bring your cube, and a little curiosity.

3
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:07,746
This is your place to learn with the club,

4
00:00:07,746 --> 00:00:08,732
practice at home,

5
00:00:08,732 --> 00:00:10,770
and take one small step at a time.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,818
You do not need an account.

7
00:00:14,818 --> 00:00:17,975
Start with a short lesson.
Speed can come later.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,140
Choose Find my starting point.

9
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:25,779
Four short questions
suggest a learning route

10
00:00:25,779 --> 00:00:27,729
based on what you can already do,

11
00:00:27,729 --> 00:00:29,800
your goals, and how you practice.

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,860
This is not a test.

13
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:37,107
If you cannot solve independently yet,

14
00:00:37,107 --> 00:00:39,182
the beginner's layer by layer route

15
00:00:39,182 --> 00:00:40,800
is a good place to start.

16
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Read the reasons, then
choose Start lesson.

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,534
You can skip the questions,

18
00:00:48,534 --> 00:00:51,120
choose a route yourself,
or change it later.

19
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,508
First, meet the moves.

20
00:00:57,508 --> 00:01:00,000
Hold white on top and green in front.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,034
U means up, D down, L left,

22
00:01:02,034 --> 00:01:04,120
R right, F front, and B back.

23
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,640
A plain letter is a
clockwise quarter turn,

24
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,500
looking straight at that face.

25
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,026
A prime means counterclockwise.

26
00:01:15,026 --> 00:01:16,750
A two means a half turn.

27
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,360
Choose U′, then Direction view.

28
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:24,200
Press Play and copy the
upper layer on your cube.

29
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,120
Replay slowly if you need.

30
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:28,720
Moving the camera only changes your view.

31
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,101
In Learn, begin with the holding

32
00:01:38,101 --> 00:01:39,820
and notation introduction.

33
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:42,460
Follow the club leader's
lesson in a meeting,

34
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:45,220
or work through the
stages at your own pace.

35
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,190
For the first cross,

36
00:01:50,190 --> 00:01:52,740
build white petals
around the yellow center.

37
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:55,553
Match each petal's side
color to its center,

38
00:01:55,553 --> 00:01:56,860
then turn it down.

39
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,935
To copy this exact example,

40
00:02:01,935 --> 00:02:04,700
open Follow along with a physical cube.

41
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:06,700
Apply its scramble from solved,

42
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,700
with white up and green front.

43
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:10,820
Our screen is already prepared.

44
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,360
Use Next move to watch one turn.

45
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,720
Read the goal and result check.

46
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:20,340
A stage jump changes only the screen;

47
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:23,120
follow all earlier
moves on your real cube.

48
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,508
Later, explore the algorithm library

49
00:02:28,508 --> 00:02:30,000
and formula practice.

50
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Learn to recognize a case
before revealing its answer.

51
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,895
Beginner and Advanced CFOP

52
00:02:34,895 --> 00:02:37,120
are there when you are ready.

53
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,068
Stuck with a cube in your hands?

54
00:02:43,068 --> 00:02:45,700
Open Solve your cube. Choose your method.

55
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,500
If you know the scramble, paste it

56
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,420
and ask for an explained solution.

57
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
This short example has
already been prepared.

58
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Follow its verified stages
with the same player.

59
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,200
Keep your cube's holding aligned,

60
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:05,120
including any shown whole cube rotations.

61
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Or choose Enter colors.

62
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,500
Copy all six faces using
each holding diagram.

63
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,700
Review them, then Check colors.

64
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:16,620
Fix any errors before
generating a solution.

65
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,320
When you can solve
independently, try Timer.

66
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:26,880
Apply the random scramble from solved.

67
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:28,515
Compare the six face diagram

68
00:03:28,515 --> 00:03:30,720
to check your cube before you begin.

69
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,642
On a keyboard, hold Space until Ready,

70
00:03:34,642 --> 00:03:36,200
then release to start.

71
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,000
Press Space again to stop.

72
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,737
This is a short control demonstration,

73
00:03:40,737 --> 00:03:42,025
not a real solve.

74
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,467
On a touch screen, hold the
large timer until Ready,

75
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:51,000
release, then touch it again to stop.

76
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,333
Optional inspection gives you time

77
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:54,750
to look before starting.

78
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,200
The history here uses
labeled example results.

79
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:05,780
See individual times,
averages of five and twelve,

80
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:07,000
and the trend.

81
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,825
You can correct a result
with plus two or DNF.

82
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Records stay in this
browser, on this device.

83
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,790
Export CSV or JSON

84
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:22,500
before clearing browser
data or changing devices.

85
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:24,900
There is no automatic cloud sync.

86
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,137
Need a reminder?

87
00:04:27,137 --> 00:04:30,680
Open Guide for screenshots
and written instructions.

88
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:34,280
Expand Every control,
explained for the details.

89
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:37,600
Page tours show the controls
right where you use them.

90
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
You can skip a step or
exit a tour at any time.

91
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,800
For today, learn one unfamiliar move,

92
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:47,750
try one lesson, and
repeat it with your cube.

93
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,320
Come back for another small step tomorrow.

94
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:55,540
Learn it here. Try it in your hands.

95
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:56,320
Your turn.
